self-administered written parental questionnaires. Analysis used grounded theory. RESULTS Main outcome measures were 
participants' views on religion/spirituality in coping with illness. Data included 632 quotes organized into 257 codes 
categorized into 11 themes. One overarching domain emerged from analysis of the 11 themes: Religious/Spiritual Coping, 
composed of 11 religious/spiritual coping strategies. CONCLUSIONS Children with CF reported a variety of 
religious/spiritual coping strategies they nearly always associated with adaptive health outcomes. A preliminary 
